<title>UK: UK gas flexibility market buys large New Year volu.</title>
<headline>UK gas flexibility market buys large New Year volu.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline arm of British Gas plc, announced on Thursday details of natural gas trade on the flexibility mechanism over the New Year.</p>
<p>On New Year's Eve there were 12 system buy bids accepted, totalling 97,395,064 kWh (3.323 million therms). The average price was 0.8357 p/kWh (24.49 pence a therm).</p>
<p>On New Year's Day, the system bought 155,248,456 kWh (5.297 million therms) in 14 lots at an average price of 0.9 p/kWh (26.38 pence a therm).</p>
<p>The highest system marginal price on either day was 1.139 p/kWh (33.38 pence a therm) on New Year's Day, a TransCo spokesman said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
